# No trailing slash, deliberately. Since the split on 2026-09-10 this is a
# SYMLINK to workbench/notes, and git treats a symlink as a file, so the
# pattern `notes/` stopped matching it. The entry then appeared as untracked
# rather than ignored, and any `git add -A` would have committed a symlink
# naming the private repository into the public one.
/notes
old_working_strips.py
venv/
.keras/
**/events.out.tfevents.*
**/lock
slurm-*.out
.hf/
.pip-cache/
venv-detect/
data/video/videonet/raw/
data/video/videonet/videos/
data/video/videonet/frames_*
# Evaluation outputs and planner exports. Data, not code.
# Model exports are the one exception and they are deliberate: there is no scp
# to Sherlock, so git is the only transport. Force-add a single export when it
# must cross machines, then untrack it once it has been consumed.
# No trailing slash. A symlink to workbench/eval since 2026-09-10; see the
# note on /notes above.
/eval

# Shell and editor files that live in the working copy but belong to the user.
.bash_profile
.bashrc
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.idea/
.mcp.json
.profile
.ripgreprc
.zprofile
.zshrc
.idea/
.venv-local/
# Also without the slash: on the cluster this is a SYMLINK to `venv`, created so
# the hardcoded `.venv-local/bin/python` in sh/gate.sh resolves there too, and a
# directory-only pattern does not match a symlink.
.venv-local

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. `settings.local.json` holds absolute paths
# -- the workstation's `/home/panoslat/...` and the cluster's
# `/scratch/users/konkotsa/panos/...` -- so it cannot be shared between the
# two. Copied across and rewritten during the 2026-09-07 migration rather than
# committed. Untracked on both machines; this only makes `git status` agree.
.claude/

# The private repository. A nested repo, not a submodule.
/workbench/
